IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `saeo-dates`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA) -- the rules a person meets who is discriminated against, sexually harassed or
-- victimised at work (or in seeking work), and who complains about it: the definitions that decide the grounds
-- (s 5(1) disability, s 5(3)-(4) caring responsibilities, s 6); what it is to discriminate on each ground (ss 29, 51,
-- 66, 85A, 85T); discrimination against workers -- applicants, employees, commission agents, independent contractors,
-- contract workers and partners -- and its exemptions (Part 3 Division 2, Part 4 Division 2, Part 5 Division 2, Part 5A
-- Division 2, Part 5B Division 2, with the general exemptions of each Part that can reach work); s 85EA (no compulsory
-- retiring age); victimisation (s 86); sexual harassment at work (s 87(1), (7), (9)); who else is liable (ss 90, 91);
-- the complaint, its time limit and extension (s 93), when the Commissioner may not proceed (s 93(4)), declining a
-- complaint (s 95A), referral to SAET or the Tribunal (s 95B), the orders (s 96), review of a refusal to extend time
-- (s 96B), appeal (s 98A), and the choice between this Act and an unfair dismissal claim (s 100).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in saeo-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "if", "unless",
-- "cannot", "does not apply", "may not", "while", a period the Act fixes); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on
-- the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. Judgments the Act leaves to others ("not reasonable in the
-- circumstances", "a substantial reason", "genuine occupational requirement", "reasonable steps", "in the opinion of the
-- Commissioner", "satisfied", "just and equitable", what the Tribunal or SAET determines) are inputs: the answer is
-- conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of South
-- Australia, CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as
-- advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (SA)`

§§ `s 5 -- disability and caring responsibilities`

-- s 5(1): "disability, in relation to a person, means -- (a) total or partial loss of the person's bodily or mental
-- functions; or (b) total or partial loss of a part of the body; or (c) the presence in the body of organisms causing
-- disease or illness; or (d) the presence in the body of organisms capable of causing disease or illness; or (e) the
-- malfunction, malformation or disfigurement of a part of the person's body; or (f) a disorder or malfunction that
-- results in the person learning differently ...; or (g) a disorder, illness or disease that affects a person's thought
-- processes, perception of reality, emotions or judgment or that results in disturbed behaviour". A "means" definition:
-- JUST FALSE when no limb holds.
DECLARE `Condition` IS ONE OF
    `total or partial loss of bodily or mental functions`
    `total or partial loss of a part of the body`
    `organisms in the body causing disease or illness`
    `organisms in the body capable of causing disease or illness`
    `malfunction, malformation or disfigurement of a part of the body`
    `a disorder or malfunction that makes me learn differently`
    `a disorder, illness or disease affecting thought, perception, emotions or judgment, or causing disturbed behaviour`
    `none of these`

GIVEN c IS A `Condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5 -- it is a disability` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 5(3): "a person has caring responsibilities if the person has responsibilities to care for or support -- (i) a
-- dependent child of the person; or (ii) any other immediate family member of the person who is in need of care and
-- support; and (b) an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person also has caring responsibilities if the person has
-- responsibilities to care for or support any person to whom that person is held to be related according to Aboriginal
-- kinship rules or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules". s 5(4): child "includes an adopted child, a step-child or an
-- ex-nuptial child"; "dependent child ... means a child who is wholly or substantially dependent on the person";
-- "immediate family member ... includes -- (a) the person's spouse or domestic partner or former spouse or former
-- domestic partner; and (b) an adult child, parent, grandparent, grandchild, or sibling of the person or of the spouse or
-- domestic partner of the person." An "if" definition: JUST FALSE when no limb holds. A relative outside the
-- "includes" list: NOTHING-kind: an unclosed list (fork F2).
DECLARE `Whom I care for` IS ONE OF
    `my child who is wholly or substantially dependent on me`
    `my spouse or domestic partner, or former spouse or domestic partner`
    `an adult child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of mine or of my spouse or domestic partner`
    `another relative`
    `a person related to me by Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules`
    `no one`

GIVEN w IS A `Whom I care for`, `the person is in need of care and support` IS A BOOLEAN, `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) -- I have caring responsibilities` w `the person is in need of care and support` `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `my child who is wholly or substantially dependent on me` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `my spouse or domestic partner, or former spouse or domestic partner` THEN
        IF `the person is in need of care and support` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an adult child, parent, grandparent, grandchild or sibling of mine or of my spouse or domestic partner` THEN
        IF `the person is in need of care and support` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another relative` THEN
        IF `the person is in need of care and support` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a person related to me by Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander kinship rules` THEN
        IF `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `no one` THEN JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 6, 29, 51, 66, 85A, 85T -- what it is to discriminate`

-- The grounds of Parts 3, 4, 5, 5A and 5B.
DECLARE `Ground` IS ONE OF
    `sex`
    `gender identity`
    `sexual orientation`
    `intersex status`
    `race`
    `disability`
    `age`
    `marital or domestic partnership status`
    `identity of my spouse or domestic partner`
    `pregnancy`
    `association with a child`
    `caring responsibilities`
    `religious appearance or dress`
    `being subjected to domestic abuse`

-- The ways the criteria sections say a person discriminates.
DECLARE `How it was done` IS ONE OF
    `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute`
    `treating me unfavourably because I cannot comply with a requirement`
    `treating me unfavourably because of a characteristic of people with the attribute`
    `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate`
    `requiring me to assume characteristics of a sex I do not identify with`
    `requiring me to alter my religious appearance or dress`
    `failing to provide safe and proper access to a place or facilities I need because of my disability`
    `treating me unfavourably because I need special access to a place or facilities`
    `failing to provide special assistance or equipment I need because of my disability`
    `treating me unfavourably because I need special assistance or equipment`
    `treating me unfavourably because of my assistance animal`

-- The facts and judgments the criteria turn on, for one act.
DECLARE `Treatment facts` HAS
    `less favourably than a person without the attribute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ground was at least a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substantially higher proportion without the attribute can comply` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `they were able to effect the access` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was unreasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the animal is an assistance animal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the appearance or dress is required by or symbolic of religious beliefs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am the perpetrator of the domestic abuse` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Grounds whose criteria have the four common limbs (direct; a requirement; a characteristic; a relative or associate):
-- ss 29(2), (2a), (3), (4), 51, 66, 85A, 85T(2), (4), (6), (8). Not s 85T(3) (identity of a spouse: one limb), s 85T(5)
-- (association with a child: the person or a relative or associate), s 85T(7) (religious appearance or dress).
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground has the four common limbs` g IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `identity of my spouse or domestic partner` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `association with a child` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `religious appearance or dress` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, h IS A `How it was done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the criteria for` g `include` h IF
    CONSIDER h
    WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `treating me unfavourably because I cannot comply with a requirement` THEN `the ground has the four common limbs` g
    WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of a characteristic of people with the attribute` THEN `the ground has the four common limbs` g
    WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate` THEN
        `the ground has the four common limbs` g
        OR g EQUALS `association with a child`
        OR g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`
    WHEN `requiring me to assume characteristics of a sex I do not identify with` THEN g EQUALS `gender identity`
    WHEN `requiring me to alter my religious appearance or dress` THEN g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`
    OTHERWISE g EQUALS `disability`

-- s 6(3): "a person ... treats another unfavourably on the basis of a particular attribute or circumstance if the
-- discriminator treats that other person less favourably than in identical or similar circumstances the discriminator
-- treats, or would treat, a person who does not have that attribute". s 6(2): "a person acts on a particular ground ...
-- if the person in fact acts on a number of grounds, one of which is the ground so referred to, and that ground is a
-- substantial reason for the act." s 6(4): a mistaken assumption is no answer (so the attribute need not be real).
-- The criteria: (a) direct; (b) a requirement "a substantially higher proportion of persons [without the attribute]
-- complies, or is able to comply, ... and ... the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances of the case";
-- (c) a characteristic that "appertains generally" to, or is "generally imputed" to, people with the attribute; (d) "an
-- attribute of or a circumstance affecting a relative or associate"; s 29(2a)(d) "requires a person of a particular
-- gender identity to assume characteristics of a sex with which the person does not identify"; s 66(ca) access "to the
-- extent that he or she is able to effect the provision of access or use"; s 66(d) "in circumstances where it is
-- unreasonable to do so"; s 66(e) an assistance animal "whether or not it is his or her normal practice"; s 85T(4)(b),
-- (c) "a pregnant woman"; s 85T(7) appearance or dress "required by, or symbolic of" religious beliefs; s 85T(8)(d)
-- "another (not being the perpetrator of domestic abuse)". Each criteria section says "a person discriminates ... if":
-- JUST FALSE when no limb holds, or when the limb is not one the ground's section has.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`, h IS A `How it was done`, f IS A `Treatment facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 6, 29, 51, 66, 85A, 85T -- they discriminated against me` g h f MEANS
    IF NOT (`the criteria for` g `include` h)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the limb is made out`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `unfavourable treatment on the ground` MEANS
            f's `less favourably than a person without the attribute` AND f's `the ground was at least a substantial reason`
        `religious` MEANS f's `the appearance or dress is required by or symbolic of religious beliefs`
        `pregnant if the ground is pregnancy` MEANS
            (NOT (g EQUALS `pregnancy`)) OR f's `I am pregnant`
        `the limb is made out` MEANS
            CONSIDER h
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground`
                AND ((NOT (g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`)) OR `religious`)
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because I cannot comply with a requirement` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground`
                AND f's `a substantially higher proportion without the attribute can comply`
                AND f's `the requirement is not reasonable in the circumstances`
                AND `pregnant if the ground is pregnancy`
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of a characteristic of people with the attribute` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground` AND `pregnant if the ground is pregnancy`
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of the attribute of a relative or associate` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground`
                AND ((NOT (g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`)) OR `religious`)
                AND ((NOT (g EQUALS `being subjected to domestic abuse`)) OR (NOT (f's `I am the perpetrator of the domestic abuse`)))
            WHEN `requiring me to assume characteristics of a sex I do not identify with` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `requiring me to alter my religious appearance or dress` THEN `religious`
            WHEN `failing to provide safe and proper access to a place or facilities I need because of my disability` THEN
                f's `they were able to effect the access`
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because I need special access to a place or facilities` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground` AND f's `they were able to effect the access`
            WHEN `failing to provide special assistance or equipment I need because of my disability` THEN
                f's `it was unreasonable in the circumstances`
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because I need special assistance or equipment` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground` AND f's `it was unreasonable in the circumstances`
            WHEN `treating me unfavourably because of my assistance animal` THEN
                `unfavourable treatment on the ground` AND f's `the animal is an assistance animal`

§§ `Part 3, 4, 5, 5A and 5B Divisions 2 -- discrimination against workers`

-- The position the person was in, or sought.
DECLARE `My position` IS ONE OF
    `someone applying for employment`
    `an employee`
    `someone seeking engagement as a commission agent`
    `a commission agent`
    `someone seeking engagement as an independent contractor`
    `an independent contractor`
    `a contract worker`
    `someone seeking to become a partner`
    `a partner`
    `none of these`

-- What was done, in the words of the work sections.
DECLARE `What was done` IS ONE OF
    `deciding who should be offered the position`
    `the terms or conditions on which the position was offered`
    `the terms or conditions of my work or membership`
    `denying or limiting access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
    `dismissing me, ending my engagement or expelling me`
    `not allowing me to work`
    `a contract or arrangement under which I am to be discriminated against`
    `subjecting me to other detriment`

-- Whether the section for the position lists what was done. ss 30(1), 31(2), 33(1), (3) (and their equivalents ss 52(1),
-- 53(2), 55(1), 67(1), 68(2), 70(1), 85B(1), 85C(2), 85E(1), 85V(1), 85W(2), 85Y(1)) for those seeking a position:
-- "in determining, or in the course of determining, who should be offered" it, and "in the terms or conditions on which"
-- it is offered. ss 30(2), 31(3), 33(4) (and equivalents) for those in a position: terms or conditions; "denying or
-- limiting access to opportunities for promotion, transfer or training, or to other benefits"; "dismissing",
-- "terminating the engagement" or "expelling"; "other detriment" (s 52(2)(d) adds segregation from persons of other
-- races, which is detriment in any event). ss 32(2), (3) (and equivalents) for contract workers: the contract or
-- arrangement; the terms or conditions on which the worker "is allowed to work"; "not allowing the contract worker to
-- work"; a benefit; other detriment.
GIVEN p IS A `My position`, w IS A `What was done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section for` p `lists` w IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a contract worker` THEN
        CONSIDER w
        WHEN `deciding who should be offered the position` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the terms or conditions on which the position was offered` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `dismissing me, ending my engagement or expelling me` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `seeking a position` p
        THEN w EQUALS `deciding who should be offered the position`
             OR w EQUALS `the terms or conditions on which the position was offered`
        ELSE w EQUALS `the terms or conditions of my work or membership`
             OR w EQUALS `denying or limiting access to promotion, transfer, training or other benefits`
             OR w EQUALS `dismissing me, ending my engagement or expelling me`
             OR w EQUALS `subjecting me to other detriment`

GIVEN p IS A `My position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `seeking a position` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `someone applying for employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone seeking engagement as a commission agent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone seeking engagement as an independent contractor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone seeking to become a partner` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ss 34(1), 56(1), 71(1), 85F(1), 85Z(1): "This Division does not apply in relation to -- (a) an employer employing a
-- person for purposes not connected with a business carried on by the employer; or (b) a principal engaging a natural
-- person as an independent contractor for purposes not connected with a business carried on by the principal." Not a
-- commission agent, a contract worker or a partner. Read to cover the applicant as well as the employee (fork F3).
GIVEN p IS A `My position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the not-connected-with-a-business exemption can reach` p IF
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `someone applying for employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `someone seeking engagement as an independent contractor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an independent contractor` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The exemptions the other side may rely on in a work case.
DECLARE `Exemption` IS ONE OF
    `none`
    `a genuine occupational requirement`
    `a religious educational institution`
    `standards of appearance and dress reasonably required`
    `I cannot do the work genuinely and reasonably required, or respond to emergencies`
    `complying with an industrial award or agreement`
    `a youth rate of pay under an award or agreement`
    `a measure intended to achieve equality`
    `a project for the benefit of people of a particular race, disability or age`
    `a body established for religious purposes`
    `a charitable instrument`
    `rates of pay for people with disabilities`
    `preventing the spread of an infectious disease`
    `unjustifiable hardship in providing access to a place or facilities`
    `rights or privileges for women in connection with pregnancy or childbirth`
    `confidentiality, conflicts of interest, nepotism, or health and safety`
    `refusing to reveal my face for identity verification`
    `caring for a child where the child lives`
    `an exemption granted by the Tribunal`

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Part 3 ground` g IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `sex` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `gender identity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sexual orientation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `intersex status` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Part 5B ground` g IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `marital or domestic partnership status` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `identity of my spouse or domestic partner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `pregnancy` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `association with a child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `caring responsibilities` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `religious appearance or dress` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `being subjected to domestic abuse` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Which grounds each exemption reaches.
-- Genuine occupational requirement: s 34(2) (Part 3 grounds), s 56(2) (race), s 85F(2) (age).
-- Religious educational institution: s 34(3) (sexual orientation, gender identity, intersex status -- not sex), and
--   s 85Z(2) (marital or domestic partnership status, against same sex domestic partners, if s 34(3) applies).
-- Appearance and dress: s 34(4) (gender identity), s 85Z(5) (religious appearance or dress).
-- Inability: s 71(2) (disability), s 85F(3) (age), s 85Z(3) (pregnancy, with (b) for a dismissal), s 85Z(4) (religious
--   appearance or dress).
-- Award compliance and youth rates: s 85F(4)(a), (b) (age).
-- Equality measures: s 47 (Part 3 grounds), s 85ZK (marital or domestic partnership status, caring responsibilities,
--   domestic abuse).
-- Projects: s 65 (race), s 82 (disability), s 85P (age).
-- Religious bodies: s 50 (Part 3 grounds), s 85ZM (marital or domestic partnership status: ordination, appointment and
--   training of priests, ministers and members of a religious order only).
-- Charitable instruments: s 45 (Part 3), s 64 (race), s 80 (disability), s 85N (age), s 85ZI (marital or domestic
--   partnership status, pregnancy, identity of a spouse or partner, caring responsibilities, domestic abuse).
-- s 84 (disability: "in relation to the provision of access to or use of a place or facilities if the provision of
-- access or use would impose unjustifiable hardship on the person"; it reaches the s 66(ca) access limbs inside the
-- work Division, and "in relation to the provision of access" is part of its conditions); s 79 and s 79A (disability); s 85ZJ (any Part 5B ground: "This Part does not render unlawful the granting to women of
-- rights or privileges in connection with pregnancy or childbirth"); s 85ZL (identity of a spouse or partner); s 85ZN
-- (religious appearance or dress); s 85ZO (domestic abuse); s 92 (any provision of the Act).
GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption`, g IS A `Ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exemption` e `reaches` g IF
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `none` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a genuine occupational requirement` THEN `a Part 3 ground` g OR g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `age`
    WHEN `a religious educational institution` THEN
        g EQUALS `sexual orientation` OR g EQUALS `gender identity` OR g EQUALS `intersex status`
        OR g EQUALS `marital or domestic partnership status`
    WHEN `standards of appearance and dress reasonably required` THEN
        g EQUALS `gender identity` OR g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`
    WHEN `I cannot do the work genuinely and reasonably required, or respond to emergencies` THEN
        g EQUALS `disability` OR g EQUALS `age` OR g EQUALS `pregnancy` OR g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`
    WHEN `complying with an industrial award or agreement` THEN g EQUALS `age`
    WHEN `a youth rate of pay under an award or agreement` THEN g EQUALS `age`
    WHEN `a measure intended to achieve equality` THEN
        `a Part 3 ground` g
        OR g EQUALS `marital or domestic partnership status`
        OR g EQUALS `caring responsibilities`
        OR g EQUALS `being subjected to domestic abuse`
    WHEN `a project for the benefit of people of a particular race, disability or age` THEN
        g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `disability` OR g EQUALS `age`
    WHEN `a body established for religious purposes` THEN
        `a Part 3 ground` g OR g EQUALS `marital or domestic partnership status`
    WHEN `a charitable instrument` THEN
        `a Part 3 ground` g OR g EQUALS `race` OR g EQUALS `disability` OR g EQUALS `age`
        OR g EQUALS `marital or domestic partnership status`
        OR g EQUALS `pregnancy`
        OR g EQUALS `identity of my spouse or domestic partner`
        OR g EQUALS `caring responsibilities`
        OR g EQUALS `being subjected to domestic abuse`
    WHEN `rates of pay for people with disabilities` THEN g EQUALS `disability`
    WHEN `preventing the spread of an infectious disease` THEN g EQUALS `disability`
    WHEN `unjustifiable hardship in providing access to a place or facilities` THEN g EQUALS `disability`
    WHEN `rights or privileges for women in connection with pregnancy or childbirth` THEN `a Part 5B ground` g
    WHEN `confidentiality, conflicts of interest, nepotism, or health and safety` THEN g EQUALS `identity of my spouse or domestic partner`
    WHEN `refusing to reveal my face for identity verification` THEN g EQUALS `religious appearance or dress`
    WHEN `caring for a child where the child lives` THEN g EQUALS `being subjected to domestic abuse`
    WHEN `an exemption granted by the Tribunal` THEN TRUE

-- Whether discrimination at work is unlawful. s 85U: Part 5B Division 2 "applies to discrimination on the ground of
-- marital or domestic partnership status, identity of spouse or domestic partner, pregnancy, caring responsibilities,
-- religious appearance or dress or being, or having been, subjected to domestic abuse" -- not association with a child:
-- NOTHING-kind: a scope limit with no "only" (finding 1). No discrimination, no position the Division names, or an act
-- the section does not list: NOTHING-kind: a prohibition limited in its own wording (other provisions may still reach
-- it). "This Division does not apply" / "This Part does not render unlawful": JUST FALSE when the exemption reaches the
-- ground and its conditions are met (the conditions, mostly judgments, are one input; see the seat's questions on
-- ss 34(3) and 85Z(3)).
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
      p IS A `My position`
      w IS A `What was done`
      `they discriminated against me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is for purposes not connected with their business` IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS AN `Exemption`
      `the exemption's conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 3-5B Division 2 -- the discrimination at work is unlawful` g p w `they discriminated against me` `the work is for purposes not connected with their business` e `the exemption's conditions are met` MEANS
    IF g EQUALS `association with a child`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF NOT `they discriminated against me`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE IF NOT (`the section for` p `lists` w)
              THEN NOTHING
              ELSE IF `the work is for purposes not connected with their business` AND `the not-connected-with-a-business exemption can reach` p
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `the exemption` e `reaches` g AND `the exemption's conditions are met`
                        THEN JUST FALSE
                        ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 34(3): "This Division does not apply to discrimination on the ground of sexual orientation, gender identity or
-- intersex status in relation to employment or engagement for the purposes of an educational institution if -- (a) the
-- educational institution is administered in accordance with the precepts of a particular religion and the
-- discrimination is founded on the precepts of that religion; and (b) the educational authority ... has a written
-- policy stating its position in relation to the matter; and (c) a copy of the policy is given to a person who is to be
-- interviewed for or offered employment ... or a teacher who is to be offered engagement as a contractor ...; and (d) a
-- copy of the policy is provided on request, free of charge" to employees, contractors, students, parents and the
-- public. s 85Z(2) carries it to marital or domestic partnership status against same sex domestic partners. "if": JUST
-- FALSE when a condition fails or the ground is not one it names.
GIVEN g IS A `Ground`
      `I am in a same sex domestic partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is for an educational institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is administered in accordance with the precepts of a religion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the discrimination is founded on those precepts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a written policy stating its position` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was given a copy before interview or offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the policy is provided on request free of charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 34(3), 85Z(2) -- the religious school exemption applies` g `I am in a same sex domestic partnership` `the work is for an educational institution` `it is administered in accordance with the precepts of a religion` `the discrimination is founded on those precepts` `it has a written policy stating its position` `I was given a copy before interview or offer` `the policy is provided on request free of charge` MEANS
    IF `the ground is reached`
       AND `the work is for an educational institution`
       AND `it is administered in accordance with the precepts of a religion`
       AND `the discrimination is founded on those precepts`
       AND `it has a written policy stating its position`
       AND `I was given a copy before interview or offer`
       AND `the policy is provided on request free of charge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the ground is reached` MEANS
            g EQUALS `sexual orientation` OR g EQUALS `gender identity` OR g EQUALS `intersex status`
            OR (g EQUALS `marital or domestic partnership status` AND `I am in a same sex domestic partnership`)

-- s 85Z(3): "This Division does not apply to discrimination against a pregnant woman on the ground of pregnancy if -- (a)
-- the discrimination is based on the fact that the woman is not, or would not be, able -- (i) to perform adequately, and
-- without endangering herself, the unborn child or other persons, the work genuinely and reasonably required of her; or
-- (ii) to respond adequately to situations of emergency ...; and (b) in the case of discrimination arising out of
-- dismissal from employment -- (i) there is no other work that the employer could reasonably be expected to offer the
-- woman; and (ii) the woman has been offered leave for the period that would result in her being unable [to do so] ...
-- and the woman has declined to take the leave." "if": JUST FALSE when a condition fails.
GIVEN `I am pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is based on my being unable to do the work safely or respond to emergencies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was no other work they could reasonably be expected to offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was offered leave for the period and declined it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85Z(3) -- the pregnancy exemption applies` `I am pregnant` `it is based on my being unable to do the work safely or respond to emergencies` `I was dismissed` `there was no other work they could reasonably be expected to offer` `I was offered leave for the period and declined it` MEANS
    IF `I am pregnant`
       AND `it is based on my being unable to do the work safely or respond to emergencies`
       AND ((NOT `I was dismissed`)
            OR (`there was no other work they could reasonably be expected to offer` AND `I was offered leave for the period and declined it`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 85EA -- no compulsory retiring age`

-- s 85EA: "Despite any Act or law to the contrary, a provision in an industrial or enterprise award, determination or
-- agreement made or approved under the Fair Work Act 1994 that -- (a) imposes, or requires or authorises an employer to
-- impose, a compulsory retiring age ...; or (b) requires or authorises an employer to terminate the employment of a
-- person on the basis of the person's age, is void and of no effect." Another instrument, or another term:
-- NOTHING-kind: the section is silent.
GIVEN `it is in an award, determination or agreement under the Fair Work Act 1994` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it imposes or authorises a compulsory retiring age, or termination because of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 85EA -- the provision is void` `it is in an award, determination or agreement under the Fair Work Act 1994` `it imposes or authorises a compulsory retiring age, or termination because of age` MEANS
    IF `it is in an award, determination or agreement under the Fair Work Act 1994` AND `it imposes or authorises a compulsory retiring age, or termination because of age`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 86 -- victimisation`

-- s 86(2): "a person commits an act of victimisation against another person (the victim) if he or she treats the victim
-- unfavourably on the ground that the victim has -- (a) brought proceedings under this Act against a person; or (b)
-- given evidence or information in proceedings under this Act; or (c) made allegations that the victim or some other
-- person has been the subject of an act that contravenes this Act; or (d) reasonably asserted the victim's right or the
-- right of some other person to lodge a complaint or take other proceedings under this Act; or (e) otherwise done
-- anything under or by reference to this Act, or on the ground that he or she knows that the victim intends to do any of
-- those things, or suspects that the victim has done, or intends to do, any of those things." (3): "Unfavourable
-- treatment on the ground that a person -- (a) has made a false allegation; or (b) has not acted in good faith, does not
-- constitute an act of victimisation." s 6(2), (3) apply. "if" and "does not constitute": JUST FALSE. The thing done
-- may be one the person did, or one the other side knew the person intended, or suspected the person had done or
-- intended: the answer is the same, so it is one input.
DECLARE `What I did under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `brought proceedings under the Act`
    `gave evidence or information in proceedings under the Act`
    `made allegations of a contravention of the Act`
    `asserted a right to complain or take proceedings under the Act`
    `did something else under or by reference to the Act`
    `none of these`

GIVEN d IS A `What I did under the Act`
      `the assertion was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was treated less favourably than someone who had not done it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that was at least a substantial reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allegation was false` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 -- I was victimised` d `the assertion was reasonable` `I was treated less favourably than someone who had not done it` `that was at least a substantial reason` `the allegation was false` `I acted in good faith` MEANS
    IF d EQUALS `none of these`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF d EQUALS `asserted a right to complain or take proceedings under the Act` AND (NOT `the assertion was reasonable`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the allegation was false` OR (NOT `I acted in good faith`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `I was treated less favourably than someone who had not done it` AND `that was at least a substantial reason`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 87 -- sexual harassment at work`

-- s 87(9)(a): "a person sexually harasses another (the person harassed) if -- (i) the person makes an unwelcome sexual
-- advance, or an unwelcome request for sexual favours, to the person harassed; or (ii) engages in other unwelcome
-- conduct of a sexual nature in relation to the person harassed, in circumstances in which a reasonable person, having
-- regard to all the circumstances, would have anticipated that the person harassed would be offended, humiliated or
-- intimidated"; (b) "conduct of a sexual nature includes making a statement of a sexual nature to a person, or in the
-- presence of a person, whether the statement is made orally or in writing". "if": JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `The conduct` IS ONE OF
    `an unwelcome sexual advance`
    `an unwelcome request for sexual favours`
    `other unwelcome conduct of a sexual nature, including a sexual statement`
    `none of these`

GIVEN c IS A `The conduct`, `a reasonable person would have anticipated I would be offended, humiliated or intimidated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(9) -- it was sexual harassment` c `a reasonable person would have anticipated I would be offended, humiliated or intimidated` MEANS
    IF (NOT (c EQUALS `none of these`)) AND `a reasonable person would have anticipated I would be offended, humiliated or intimidated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 87(1): "It is unlawful for a person to subject to sexual harassment -- (a) a person with whom he or she works; or (b)
-- a person who is seeking to become a fellow worker, while in attendance at a place that is a workplace of both the
-- persons or in circumstances where the person was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware that the other person was a
-- fellow worker or seeking to become a fellow worker." (9)(c): "a person works with another if both carry out duties or
-- perform functions, in whatever capacity and whether for payment or not, in or in relation to the same business or
-- organisation"; (e) "workplace means a place (including a ship, aircraft or vehicle) at which a person works or
-- attends in connection with the person's work." Not harassment, or neither (a) nor (b): NOTHING-kind: a prohibition
-- limited in its own wording (other subsections, or s 87(7), may reach it). The "while ... or in circumstances where"
-- fails: JUST FALSE (fork F4).
DECLARE `How we are connected at work` IS ONE OF
    `we carry out duties for the same business or organisation`
    `I was seeking to become their fellow worker`
    `neither`

GIVEN `it was sexual harassment` IS A BOOLEAN
      k IS A `How we are connected at work`
      `it was at a place that is a workplace of us both` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were or ought reasonably to have been aware of the connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(1) -- the sexual harassment at work was unlawful` `it was sexual harassment` k `it was at a place that is a workplace of us both` `they were or ought reasonably to have been aware of the connection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it was sexual harassment`) OR k EQUALS `neither`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `it was at a place that is a workplace of us both` OR `they were or ought reasonably to have been aware of the connection`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 87(7): "If an employee reports to his or her employer specific circumstances in which the employee was subjected, in
-- the course of his or her employment, to sexual harassment by a person other than a fellow worker, and it is reasonable
-- in all the circumstances to expect that further sexual harassment of the employee by the same person is likely to
-- occur, it is unlawful for the employer to fail to take reasonable steps to prevent the further sexual harassment."
-- A duty whose "if" is unmet: JUST FALSE (fork F5). The steps having been taken: JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `I was sexually harassed in the course of my employment by someone who is not a fellow worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I reported the specific circumstances to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `further harassment by the same person is reasonably to be expected` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employer took reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87(7) -- my employer's failure to prevent further harassment is unlawful` `I was sexually harassed in the course of my employment by someone who is not a fellow worker` `I reported the specific circumstances to my employer` `further harassment by the same person is reasonably to be expected` `my employer took reasonable steps to prevent it` MEANS
    IF `I was sexually harassed in the course of my employment by someone who is not a fellow worker`
       AND `I reported the specific circumstances to my employer`
       AND `further harassment by the same person is reasonably to be expected`
       AND (NOT `my employer took reasonable steps to prevent it`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 90, 91 -- who else is liable`

-- s 91(1): "Subject to this section, a person is, for the purposes of this Act, vicariously liable for a discriminatory or
-- unlawful act of an agent or employee of the person committed while acting in the course of their agency or
-- employment." (2): "it is a defence to prove that the person took reasonable steps to ensure that the agent or employee
-- would not act in contravention of this Act." (3): "Without limiting subsection (2), a defence is established ... if the
-- person -- (a) had in force at the relevant time an appropriate policy for the prevention of such an act; and (b) had
-- taken reasonable steps to implement and enforce the policy including -- (i) reasonable steps to make the employees and
-- agents of the person aware of the terms of the policy; and (ii) prompt investigation of any alleged act and taking
-- appropriate action." Not an act of their employee or agent in the course of the employment or agency: NOTHING-kind:
-- the section is limited in its own wording (they may be liable directly). A defence proved: JUST FALSE ("this section
-- gives no liability on these facts"). (3)(b)(i) and (ii) read as required parts of (b) (fork F6).
GIVEN `the act was done by their employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was done in the course of the employment or agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they prove they took reasonable steps to prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they had an appropriate prevention policy in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they took reasonable steps to implement and enforce it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they took reasonable steps to make staff aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they promptly investigated and acted on alleged acts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 -- they are vicariously liable` `the act was done by their employee or agent` `it was done in the course of the employment or agency` `they prove they took reasonable steps to prevent it` `they had an appropriate prevention policy in force` `they took reasonable steps to implement and enforce it` `they took reasonable steps to make staff aware of it` `they promptly investigated and acted on alleged acts` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the act was done by their employee or agent`) OR (NOT `it was done in the course of the employment or agency`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `they prove they took reasonable steps to prevent it` OR `the s 91(3) defence is made out`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the s 91(3) defence is made out` MEANS
            `they had an appropriate prevention policy in force`
            AND `they took reasonable steps to implement and enforce it`
            AND `they took reasonable steps to make staff aware of it`
            AND `they promptly investigated and acted on alleged acts`

-- s 90: "If a person causes, instructs, induces or aids another to act in contravention of this Act, both are jointly and
-- severally liable to any criminal or civil liability arising under this Act in respect of the contravention."
-- Otherwise: NOTHING-kind: the section is silent.
GIVEN `there was a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `they caused, instructed, induced or aided it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90 -- they are jointly and severally liable` `there was a contravention` `they caused, instructed, induced or aided it` MEANS
    IF `there was a contravention` AND `they caused, instructed, induced or aided it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulative rules -- steps that must be taken in time`

-- "A complaint must be lodged ... within 12 months" (s 93(2)); "An application for review must be made within 1 month
-- after notification of the decision" (s 96B(2)); "the complainant has, within 3 months of being notified of the
-- Commissioner's decision, by notice in writing, required the Commissioner to refer the complaint to the Tribunal"
-- (s 95B(1)(c)); "the complainant contacts the Commissioner within 12 months after the date of that determination
-- requesting that the complaint proceed" (s 95A(3)(b)). Each rule starts at 0 and allows a number of days; FULFILLED
-- means in time. They take DEONTIC values, so they are never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `lodge the complaint`
    `apply for review of the refusal to extend time`
    `require the Commissioner to refer the complaint`
    `ask the Commissioner to reinstate the complaint`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 93(2) -- the complaint must be lodged within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `lodge the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "s 93(2): a complaint must be lodged within 12 months of the contravention, or of the last of a series of acts, unless the Commissioner extends the time"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 96B(2) -- the review application must be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `apply for review of the refusal to extend time`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "s 96B(2): an application for review of a refusal to extend time must be made within 1 month after notification of the decision"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 95B(1)(c) -- the referral must be required within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `require the Commissioner to refer the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "s 95B(1)(c): a declined complaint goes to the Tribunal only if the complainant requires it by written notice within 3 months of being notified of the decision"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`s 95A(3) -- the request to proceed must be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `ask the Commissioner to reinstate the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "s 95A(3): the Commissioner may reinstate the complaint only if the complainant asks within 12 months after the determination"

-- Whether a party taking a step at a time satisfies a rule.
GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the party` IS A `Party`, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `taking the step at` `the time of the step` `by` `the party` `the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the party` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether a step taken on a day is in time for a deadline that runs from a start day to a last day (both counted). A
-- day before the start is in time.
GIVEN `the day of the step` IS A DATE, `the start day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE, `the step` IS A `Step`, `the rule maker` IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a step on` `the day of the step` `is in time from` `the start day` `to` `the last day` `for` `the step` `under` `the rule maker` IF
    IF `the day of the step` `is before` `the start day`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `taking the step at` (`the days from` `the start day` `to` `the day of the step`) `by` `the complainant` `the step` `satisfies` (`the rule maker` (`the days from` `the start day` `to` `the last day`))

§§ `s 93 -- the complaint`

-- s 93(2): "(a) if the alleged contravention is constituted of a series of acts -- within 12 months of the last of those
-- acts; (b) in any other case -- within 12 months of the date on which the contravention is alleged to have been
-- committed." "Of the date" excludes the day: the last day is the same day 12 months later (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the act, or the last act of the series` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 93(2) -- the last day to lodge` `the day of the act, or the last act of the series` MEANS
    `the date` 12 `months after` `the day of the act, or the last act of the series`

-- s 93(2a): "The Commissioner may, on application, extend the time for lodging a complaint, even if the time ... has
-- expired, if the Commissioner is satisfied -- (a) that there is good reason why the complaint was not made within the
-- stipulated time period; and (b) that in all the circumstances it is just and equitable to do so." The power exists
-- only "if": JUST FALSE otherwise. Whether it is used is the Commissioner's discretion (an input below).
GIVEN `I applied for an extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied there is good reason for the delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it is just and equitable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(2a) -- the Commissioner may extend the time` `I applied for an extension` `the Commissioner is satisfied there is good reason for the delay` `the Commissioner is satisfied it is just and equitable` MEANS
    IF `I applied for an extension` AND `the Commissioner is satisfied there is good reason for the delay` AND `the Commissioner is satisfied it is just and equitable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 93(2) with (2a): in time if lodged by the last day (the s 93(2) rule, by trace), or if the Commissioner has extended
-- the time; otherwise JUST FALSE (a period the Act fixes).
GIVEN `the day of the act, or the last act of the series` IS A DATE
      `the day I lodge` IS A DATE
      `the Commissioner extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(2) -- my complaint is in time` `the day of the act, or the last act of the series` `the day I lodge` `the Commissioner extended the time` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner extended the time`
       OR `a step on` `the day I lodge` `is in time from` `the day of the act, or the last act of the series` `to` (`s 93(2) -- the last day to lodge` `the day of the act, or the last act of the series`) `for` `lodge the complaint` `under` `s 93(2) -- the complaint must be lodged within`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 93(1): "A complaint alleging that a person has acted in contravention of this Act may be made -- (a) by a person
-- aggrieved by the act; (b) by a person aggrieved by the act, on behalf of himself or herself and any other person
-- aggrieved by the act; (c) if a person aggrieved by the act is a child or has an intellectual disability -- by a person
-- who is, in the opinion of the Commissioner, a suitable representative of the interests of the aggrieved person."
-- (1a): "A person cannot make a complaint pursuant to subsection (1)(b) on behalf of some other person unless that other
-- person has consented in writing". (1c): "A complaint -- (a) must be in writing and set out the details of the alleged
-- contravention; and (b) must be lodged with the Commissioner." (2): the time. Someone not aggrieved and not a
-- representative: NOTHING-kind: a list not closed by "only" (fork F7). (1a) "cannot ... unless": JUST FALSE. (1c) not
-- met: JUST FALSE (a bare "must" not done; fork F7). (2) out of time and not extended: JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Who complains` IS ONE OF
    `I, as a person aggrieved`
    `I, for myself and others aggrieved`
    `I, as representative of an aggrieved child or person with an intellectual disability`
    `someone who is none of these`

GIVEN w IS A `Who complains`
      `the others have consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner thinks me a suitable representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in writing with the details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is lodged with the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in time` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93 -- the complaint may be made` w `the others have consented in writing` `the Commissioner thinks me a suitable representative` `it is in writing with the details` `it is lodged with the Commissioner` `in time` MEANS
    IF w EQUALS `someone who is none of these`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF w EQUALS `I, for myself and others aggrieved` AND (NOT `the others have consented in writing`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF w EQUALS `I, as representative of an aggrieved child or person with an intellectual disability` AND (NOT `the Commissioner thinks me a suitable representative`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF (NOT `it is in writing with the details`) OR (NOT `it is lodged with the Commissioner`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE `in time`

-- s 93(4): "if the Commissioner becomes aware that -- (a) a criminal investigation is being conducted in relation to a
-- matter that is the subject of a complaint; or (b) a person has been or is to be charged with a criminal offence ...,
-- the Commissioner may not proceed to investigate or otherwise deal with the complaint ... or to attempt to resolve [it]
-- by conciliation, until the criminal investigation has been completed or the proceedings for the offence have been
-- disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed." An "until" bar: JUST TRUE (the Commissioner may proceed) when no bar,
-- JUST FALSE while it stands.
GIVEN `a criminal investigation of the matter is under way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone has been or is to be charged, and the charge is not disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93(4) -- the Commissioner may deal with my complaint now` `a criminal investigation of the matter is under way` `someone has been or is to be charged, and the charge is not disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed` MEANS
    IF `a criminal investigation of the matter is under way` OR `someone has been or is to be charged, and the charge is not disposed of, withdrawn or permanently stayed`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 96B(2): "within 1 month after notification of the decision" (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day I was notified of the refusal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 96B(2) -- the last day to apply for review` `the day I was notified of the refusal` MEANS
    `the date` 1 `months after` `the day I was notified of the refusal`

-- s 96B(1), (2): the applicant "may apply to the Tribunal ... for a review" of a refusal to extend time; "must be made
-- within 1 month". No refusal: NOTHING-kind: the section does not arise. Late: JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the Commissioner refused to extend my time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was notified of the refusal` IS A DATE
      `the day I apply for review` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96B -- I may apply for review of the refusal` `the Commissioner refused to extend my time` `the day I was notified of the refusal` `the day I apply for review` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Commissioner refused to extend my time`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `a step on` `the day I apply for review` `is in time from` `the day I was notified of the refusal` `to` (`s 96B(2) -- the last day to apply for review` `the day I was notified of the refusal`) `for` `apply for review of the refusal to extend time` `under` `s 96B(2) -- the review application must be made within`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 95A, 95B -- declining and referring my complaint`

-- s 95A(1): "The Commissioner may, by notice in writing to the complainant, decline to recognise a complaint as one on
-- which action should be taken ... if, in the opinion of the Commissioner -- (a) the complaint is frivolous, vexatious,
-- misconceived or lacking in substance; or (b) the complaint has ceased to be a complaint that should be proceeded with
-- because the complainant -- (i) has died; or (ii) is unable to be contacted; or (iii) has expressed an intention not to
-- proceed, or otherwise evidenced a lack of interest ...; or (iv) has unreasonably refused or failed to cooperate; or (c)
-- there is no reasonable prospect of an order being made by the Tribunal under section 96(1) or of an order ... more
-- favourable to the complainant than offers refused by the complainant in conciliation proceedings; or (d) the
-- complaint alleges discrimination on the ground of being, or having been, subjected to domestic abuse and the
-- complainant fails to provide sufficient evidence that they are, or have been, subjected to domestic abuse." (4):
-- sufficient evidence is "(a) evidence that an intervention order has been issued ...; or (b) evidence that the
-- complainant has sought or received assistance in relation to domestic abuse from -- (i) a registered health
-- practitioner; or (ii) a charitable organisation; or (iii) a person or body of a class prescribed by the regulations
-- [none deposited; asked as a fact]; or (c) evidence that otherwise satisfies the Commissioner". The power exists only
-- "if": JUST FALSE when no ground holds.
DECLARE `My evidence of domestic abuse` IS ONE OF
    `an intervention order protecting me`
    `help I sought or received from a registered health practitioner`
    `help I sought or received from a charitable organisation`
    `help I sought or received from a prescribed person or body`
    `other evidence that satisfies the Commissioner`
    `none`

GIVEN `the Commissioner thinks it frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner thinks I have stopped pursuing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner thinks there is no reasonable prospect of an order, or of a better one than offers I refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my complaint is of domestic abuse discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN
      v IS A `My evidence of domestic abuse`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(1) -- the Commissioner may decline my complaint` `the Commissioner thinks it frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance` `the Commissioner thinks I have stopped pursuing it` `the Commissioner thinks there is no reasonable prospect of an order, or of a better one than offers I refused` `my complaint is of domestic abuse discrimination` v MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner thinks it frivolous, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance`
       OR `the Commissioner thinks I have stopped pursuing it`
       OR `the Commissioner thinks there is no reasonable prospect of an order, or of a better one than offers I refused`
       OR (`my complaint is of domestic abuse discrimination` AND v EQUALS `none`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 95A(3): "If -- (a) the Commissioner has determined that a complaint has ceased to be a complaint that should be
-- proceeded with under subsection (1)(b); and (b) the complainant contacts the Commissioner within 12 months after the
-- date of that determination requesting that the complaint proceed, the Commissioner may reinstate the complaint."
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 95A(3) -- the last day to ask to proceed` `the day of the determination` MEANS
    `the date` 12 `months after` `the day of the determination`

GIVEN `it was declined because I stopped pursuing it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
      `the day I ask to proceed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95A(3) -- the Commissioner may reinstate my complaint` `it was declined because I stopped pursuing it` `the day of the determination` `the day I ask to proceed` MEANS
    IF `it was declined because I stopped pursuing it`
       AND `a step on` `the day I ask to proceed` `is in time from` `the day of the determination` `to` (`s 95A(3) -- the last day to ask to proceed` `the day of the determination`) `for` `ask the Commissioner to reinstate the complaint` `under` `s 95A(3) -- the request to proceed must be made within`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 95B(1)(c): "within 3 months of being notified of the Commissioner's decision" (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day I was notified it was declined` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 95B(1)(c) -- the last day to require referral` `the day I was notified it was declined` MEANS
    `the date` 3 `months after` `the day I was notified it was declined`

-- s 95B(1): "If, in respect of a complaint, the Commissioner -- (a) is of the opinion that the matter cannot be resolved
-- by conciliation; or (b) has attempted to resolve the matter by conciliation but has not been successful ...; or (ba)
-- is of the opinion that the matter should be transferred ...; or (c) has declined to recognise the complaint ... and
-- the complainant has, within 3 months of being notified of the Commissioner's decision, by notice in writing, required
-- the Commissioner to refer the complaint to the Tribunal, the Commissioner must refer the matter to the Tribunal for
-- hearing and determination." A declined complaint without a written notice in time: JUST FALSE (the period). A
-- complaint still in conciliation, or resolved: NOTHING-kind: the duty has not arisen.
DECLARE `Where my complaint stands` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner thinks it cannot be resolved by conciliation`
    `conciliation was tried and failed`
    `the Commissioner thinks it should be transferred`
    `the Commissioner declined it`
    `it is still being dealt with or was resolved`

GIVEN s IS A `Where my complaint stands`
      `I required referral by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was notified it was declined` IS A DATE
      `the day of my notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95B(1) -- the Commissioner must refer my complaint` s `I required referral by written notice` `the day I was notified it was declined` `the day of my notice` MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `it is still being dealt with or was resolved` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the Commissioner declined it` THEN
        IF `I required referral by written notice`
           AND `a step on` `the day of my notice` `is in time from` `the day I was notified it was declined` `to` (`s 95B(1)(c) -- the last day to require referral` `the day I was notified it was declined`) `for` `require the Commissioner to refer the complaint` `under` `s 95B(1)(c) -- the referral must be required within`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 95B(2): "if ... the matter involves -- (a) an alleged contravention of Part 3 Division 2, Part 4 Division 2, Part 5
-- Division 2, Part 5A Division 2 or Part 5B Division 2; or (b) an alleged contravention of section 86, 87 or 88 by a
-- person against -- (i) a person with whom they work; or (ii) a person who is seeking to become a fellow worker, the
-- Commissioner must not refer the matter to the Tribunal ... but must instead refer the matter to SAET". (2a): "both
-- alleged contraventions of a kind referred to in subsection (2) and other matters, the Commissioner may refer the
-- matter to SAET or to the Tribunal, as the Commissioner thinks fit."
DECLARE `Forum` IS ONE OF
    `SAET`
    `the Tribunal (SACAT)`
    `SAET or the Tribunal, as the Commissioner thinks fit`

GIVEN `it involves discrimination against a worker under a Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves victimisation, sexual harassment or an assistance animal, by someone I work with or sought to work with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it also involves other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Forum`
`s 95B(2), (2a) -- where my complaint is referred` `it involves discrimination against a worker under a Division 2` `it involves victimisation, sexual harassment or an assistance animal, by someone I work with or sought to work with` `it also involves other matters` MEANS
    IF `it involves discrimination against a worker under a Division 2` OR `it involves victimisation, sexual harassment or an assistance animal, by someone I work with or sought to work with`
    THEN IF `it also involves other matters`
         THEN `SAET or the Tribunal, as the Commissioner thinks fit`
         ELSE `SAET`
    ELSE `the Tribunal (SACAT)`

§§ `s 96 -- the orders`

-- s 96(1): "on determining that the respondent ... has acted in contravention of this Act, make one or more of the
-- following orders: (a) subject to this section, an order requiring the respondent to pay compensation (of such amount
-- as the Tribunal thinks fit) to a person for loss or damage arising from the contravention; (b) an order requiring the
-- respondent to refrain from further contravention of the Act; (c) an order requiring the respondent or any other party
-- ... to perform specified acts with a view to redressing loss or damage ... or remedying a discriminatory or unlawful
-- act." (2): "at any stage of proceedings ... (a) make an interim order to prevent prejudice to a person affected by the
-- proceedings; (b) make an order dismissing the proceedings." (3): damage "includes injury to his or her feelings". (3a):
-- other awards "must" be taken into account. (3b): "An award of compensation may not be made against a child for an act
-- in contravention of this Act (but an award of compensation may be made against a person who is vicariously liable for
-- the act of the child)." No cap. SAET has the same powers when the matter is referred to it (s 95B(3)). Before a
-- contravention is determined, the (1) orders: NOTHING-kind: the power has not arisen. Against a child: JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `compensation, including for injury to feelings`
    `an order to refrain from further contravention`
    `an order to perform specified acts to redress the loss or remedy the act`
    `an interim order to prevent prejudice`

GIVEN o IS AN `Order`
      `the tribunal has determined the respondent contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is a child` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96 -- the tribunal may make the order` o `the tribunal has determined the respondent contravened the Act` `the respondent is a child` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `an interim order to prevent prejudice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `compensation, including for injury to feelings` THEN
        IF `the respondent is a child`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the tribunal has determined the respondent contravened the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the tribunal has determined the respondent contravened the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 98A -- appeal`

-- s 98A(1): "A right of appeal lies to the Supreme Court against -- (a) a decision by the Tribunal on an application for
-- the grant, renewal or revocation of an exemption; or (b) a decision or order made by the Tribunal in proceedings under
-- this Part." (2): "An appeal under this section may be made by a party to the proceedings". Not a party, or another
-- decision: NOTHING-kind: the section is limited in its own wording (the SACAT Act may give another route).
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision or order in the proceedings on my complaint`
    `a decision on an application for an exemption`
    `another decision`

GIVEN d IS A `The decision`, `I am a party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98A(1), (2) -- I may appeal to the Supreme Court` d `I am a party to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `I am a party to the proceedings` AND (NOT (d EQUALS `another decision`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 98A(3)(b): "if the reasons of the Tribunal were not given in writing at the time of the making of a decision or order
-- and the appellant then requested the Tribunal to state its reasons in writing, the time for instituting the appeal
-- under section 71 of the South Australian Civil and Administrative Tribunal Act 2013 runs from the time when the written
-- statement of those reasons is given to the appellant". Otherwise the start is set by the SACAT Act, outside this
-- encoding: NOTHING-kind: points outside the sources.
GIVEN `written reasons were given when the decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I then asked for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the written reasons were given to me` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 98A(3)(b) -- the day my appeal time runs from` `written reasons were given when the decision was made` `I then asked for written reasons` `the day the written reasons were given to me` MEANS
    IF (NOT `written reasons were given when the decision was made`) AND `I then asked for written reasons`
    THEN JUST `the day the written reasons were given to me`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 100 -- this Act or an unfair dismissal claim`

-- s 100(2): "If a person brings proceedings under -- (a) Chapter 3 Part 6 of the Fair Work Act 1994; or (b) Part 3-2 of
-- the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth, in respect of dismissal from employment, and those proceedings are
-- determined, that person cannot institute or prosecute proceedings under this Act in respect of that dismissal." (3):
-- "Subsection (2) does not apply if the proceedings under the Fair Work Act 1994 or the Fair Work Act 2009 of the
-- Commonwealth are dismissed on a ground that does not relate to a ground of discrimination under this Act." Barred:
-- JUST TRUE. The "if" unmet, or (3): JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `I brought unfair dismissal proceedings about the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were dismissed on a ground unrelated to a ground of discrimination under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(2), (3) -- I am barred from proceedings under this Act` `I brought unfair dismissal proceedings about the dismissal` `they were determined` `they were dismissed on a ground unrelated to a ground of discrimination under this Act` MEANS
    IF `I brought unfair dismissal proceedings about the dismissal` AND `they were determined` AND (NOT `they were dismissed on a ground unrelated to a ground of discrimination under this Act`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 100(4): "If a person brings proceedings under this Act in respect of dismissal from employment, and those
-- proceedings are determined, that person cannot institute or prosecute proceedings under the Fair Work Act 1994 in
-- respect of the dismissal." (5): "Subsection (4) does not apply if the proceedings under this Act are dismissed and the
-- proceedings under the Fair Work Act 1994 do not relate to a ground of discrimination under this Act." s 100(4) names
-- only the State Act: a claim under the Fair Work Act 2009 (Cth): NOTHING-kind: the section is silent (finding 4).
GIVEN `I brought proceedings under this Act about the dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my unfair dismissal claim relates to a ground of discrimination under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my unfair dismissal claim is under the Commonwealth Fair Work Act 2009` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(4), (5) -- I am barred from an unfair dismissal claim` `I brought proceedings under this Act about the dismissal` `they were determined` `they were dismissed` `my unfair dismissal claim relates to a ground of discrimination under this Act` `my unfair dismissal claim is under the Commonwealth Fair Work Act 2009` MEANS
    IF `my unfair dismissal claim is under the Commonwealth Fair Work Act 2009`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `I brought proceedings under this Act about the dismissal` AND `they were determined`
         THEN IF `they were dismissed` AND (NOT `my unfair dismissal claim relates to a ground of discrimination under this Act`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE
